{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>Who…</b> The Gaon [Saadia] said that he did not mention the Spirit among the three foundations, and he said that the Name is the answer, as if he said, \"Who measured the Spirit?\" — and the answer is the Name. In my opinion this is not correct, because the verse reads את רוח, and the meaning is: who informed us His counsel? And so its interpretation is: who measured the Spirit of HaShem? And he attached the Spirit to Him, like ורוח אלהים מרחפת (Genesis 1:2). And the first מי draws after it [another], and [the second] מי [means] — who is the man who informs us HaShem's counsel, why He created thus:"], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 40, :notes {0 "Resolved 'השלשה המוסדים' as 'the three foundations'; 'השם תשובה' read as 'the Name is the answer.' The final clause למה ברא כן is taken as a hyper-literal rendering of the Hebrew as it stands."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:57:09.464315109Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}